The teal figure on the star court is chr_robot_gardener (env_skycity.glb, anchor_robot_root, 4.0 m from
anchor_starcourt_center), animated by RegionAmbientAnimation (robot_idle + sky_ambient_loop). It is part of the region
model, so both the journey copy and the board copy have it; no code hides it (the board_bgonly capture shows it, and
运镜bot's strips show it in every journey frame -10..-1; on the board it sits behind the board tray). What did differ:
each copy ran its ambient clips from its own start, so on the swap frame the robot (and the sky clouds / rocks / birds)
jumped to another phase. withRegionBoardGuest now, on the board's first setVisible(true), puts every clip playing on the
journey copy on the same time on the board copy (syncRegionAmbient, sampled). Lease files untouched.
Test: region-board-ambient (real GLB: robot node + clips; nothing singles out the robot; sync on first show only;
no journey copy / journey gone -> unchanged, no throw).
